From: KmsLocks <kmslocks@local>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 08:00:00 
Subject: [PATCH 0121] gpu31-kms: simplify drm_modeset_lock_all for bring-up and log it (int77)

After int76 the device loads and the DECON IRQs run, but every userspace entry
blocks in drm_modeset_lock_all (modetest drm_mode_getresources) or in
fb_open's info->lock, i.e. a modeset lock stayed held after the initial
modeset.

  - drm_modeset_lock_all() no longer takes connection_mutex or the per-object
    w/w crtc/plane modeset locks; it keeps mode_config.mutex + the legacy
    crtc->mutex loop and still installs config->acquire_ctx (used by
    drm_atomic_helper_set_config() as state->acquire_ctx; any w/w locks the
    commit path adds to it are dropped by unlock_all()).
    This is a bring-up simplification to revisit before multiple
    drivers/clients (documented in the code).
  - lock_all/unlock_all log the caller (current->comm) and the ctx pointer, so
    an enter without a matching exit names the leaking path.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_crtc.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_crtc.c
@@ -57,6 +57,7 @@
 	if (WARN_ON(!ctx))
 		return;
 
+	pr_info("drm_modeset_lock_all: enter by %s (ctx=%p)\n", current->comm, config->acquire_ctx);
 	mutex_lock(&config->mutex);
 
 	drm_modeset_acquire_init(ctx, 0);
@@ -64,20 +65,20 @@
 	list_for_each_entry(crtc, &config->crtc_list, head)
 		mutex_lock_nest_lock(&crtc->mutex, &config->mutex);
 
-	ret = drm_modeset_lock(&config->connection_mutex, ctx);
-	if (!ret)
-		ret = drm_modeset_lock_all_crtcs(dev, ctx);
-	if (WARN_ON(ret)) {
-		drm_modeset_drop_locks(ctx);
-		drm_modeset_acquire_fini(ctx);
-		kfree(ctx);
-		list_for_each_entry(crtc, &config->crtc_list, head)
-			mutex_unlock(&crtc->mutex);
-		mutex_unlock(&config->mutex);
-		return;
-	}
+	/*
+	 * int77 (bring-up simplification): do NOT take connection_mutex or the
+	 * per-object w/w modeset locks here.  The 4.0 expansion is what
+	 * drm_mode_getresources blocked on after the initial modeset, and with
+	 * a single driver and the legacy crtc->mutex already held the extra
+	 * locks buy nothing.  Revisit before multiple drivers/clients.
+	 * The acquire ctx is still installed because
+	 * drm_atomic_helper_set_config() uses it as state->acquire_ctx and the
+	 * commit path adds crtc/plane w/w locks to it; unlock_all drops those.
+	 */
+	ret = 0;
 
 	WARN_ON(config->acquire_ctx);
+	pr_info("drm_modeset_lock_all: acquired by %s (config->acquire_ctx=%p)\n", current->comm, ctx);
 
 	/*
 	 * now we hold the locks, so now that it is safe, stash the ctx for
@@ -98,6 +99,7 @@
 	struct drm_modeset_acquire_ctx *ctx = config->acquire_ctx;
 	struct drm_crtc *crtc;
 
+	pr_info("drm_modeset_unlock_all: enter by %s (config->acquire_ctx=%p)\n", current->comm, ctx);
 	if (WARN_ON(!ctx)) {
 		mutex_unlock(&config->mutex);
 		return;
